msgid "ZED stereo camera for Non-GPS Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:12
#: a8b6c9ba11704c2ea0b90d41c5a5afdd
msgid "This article explains how a `ZED stereo camera <https://www.stereolabs.com>`__ can be used with `OpenKai <https://github.com/yankailab/OpenKAI>`__ as a substitute for a GPS allowing position control modes like Loiter, PosHold, RTL, Auto."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:18
#: 5cf1787637814ad8a1bc388df3a15168
msgid "Required Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:20
#: c432e16ead1c4888a7253bd6100c9569
msgid "`Stereo Labs ZED camera <https://store.stereolabs.com/products/zed>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:21
#: c3a4505dfb6644f581908b6bff9cab4d
msgid "`NVidia TX1 <https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/autonomous-machines/embedded-systems-dev-kits-modules/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:22
#: 35638c827a144c799d25b7302e6bd2b4
msgid "`Auvidea J120 carrier board <https://auvidea.com/j120/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:25
#: 198e7a97c9b34278b374f4784fdbde0a
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:27
#: dc85ccab7a344999ba6a388121cd9922
msgid "connect the autopilot and TX1 as shown on the `NVidia TX1 as a Companion Computer <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.html>`__ wiki page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:28
#: c8aba6fa415f4c5ab1b3b1d2c26448f1
msgid "flash the TX1 as described in the `Setup the TX1 <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.html#setup-the-tx1>`__ section of the above wiki page but use the apsync-tx1-openkai image from `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Companion/apsync/beta/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:29
#: 0dfeaf891b9c45a0a83c231b14ab7a1c
msgid "mount the ZED camera upside-down and using vibration dampeners to the front of the vehicle. It can be mounted right-side-up after `connecting with ssh <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/apsync-intro.html#connecting-with-ssh>`__ and then modify `~/src/OpenKAI/kiss/apmCopter.kiss <https://github.com/yankailab/OpenKAI/blob/master/kiss/apmCopter.kiss#L60>`__ so \"bFlip\" is `1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:31
#: e8b5180bebef4cbd80802ad6e14d9e25
msgid "in order to download the ZED camera's calibration parameters from stereolabs.com, connect the TX1 to the Internet with an Ethernet cable during powerup (this procedure is only required once)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:32
#: 4fa1f61bc69f42b78d3bc3f8e9c8d9e9
msgid "disable APSync's video streaming (so that OpenKai can use the camera) by connecting your computer to APSync's access point (``ssid=ardupilot``, pw=ardupilot), then open a browser to ``http://10.0.1.128:8000`` and click the red **Disable Auto Streaming** button (button should turn green) and reboot the TX1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:40
#: 340005564a2b4253a7123f22e76603cd
msgid "Configuration through the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:41
#: 09f2407fea724dff8d4fb866a2d014d7
msgid "Example setup below shown for first proximity sensor:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:43
#: 0471a1b197e545af9948b0dd0f4427e6
msgid "enable communication between the TX1 and autopilot using the `Setup the Pixhawk instructions from the tx1 setup wiki page <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx1.html#setup-the-pixhawk>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:44
#: 1e1448b3ecbd42f0beaa451bbea6813f
msgid "set :ref:`AHRS_EKF_TYPE <AHRS_EKF_TYPE>` to 3 (means use EKF3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:45
#: f9de38c44e3b406590838f6ff1054498
msgid "set :ref:`EK2_ENABLE <EK2_ENABLE>` to 0 (disable EKF2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:46
#: 454835e87f674c3f9159b735d9bbb3e5
msgid "set :ref:`EK3_ENABLE <EK3_ENABLE>` to 1 (enable EKF3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:47
#: 361b85840c51423b808e852aff3cf230
msgid "set :ref:`GPS1_TYPE <GPS1_TYPE>` to 0 (disable the GPS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:48
#: f4d3bafc86894fa9bee3b8a2631d491e
msgid "set :ref:`VISO_TYPE <VISO_TYPE>` to 1 (enable visual odometry)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:49
#: f3ceab68c1014bafbe03427d89f49727
msgid "optionally set :ref:`PRX1_TYPE <PRX1_TYPE>` to 2 (enable using ZED's depth map for object avoidance)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:51
#: 65ca291edf6245c8a15ad3b14f2831d3
msgid "Optionally you may also:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:53
#: 73e1230a0e02406780b6e218017133c1
msgid "set the :ref:`VISO_POS_X <VISO_POS_X>`, :ref:`VISO_POS_Y  <VISO_POS_Y>` and :ref:`VISO_POS_Z  <VISO_POS_Z>` to account for the camera's offset from the IMU or vehicle's center-of-gravity (:ref:`more details here <common-sensor-offset-compensation>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:54
#: 96f0e99aa40e4d2190d64fd7925f4ba9
msgid "mount the camera in other orientations and change the :ref:`VISO_ORIENT <VISO_ORIENT>` parameter. Note: if you are using the ZED's depth sensing you will also need to modify `OpenKai's configuration <https://github.com/yankailab/OpenKAI/blob/master/kiss/apmCopter.kiss>`__  (not documented)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:58
#: cbb17461337948e1a242b17626f374bf
msgid "Ground Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:60
#: 1932da1323d34f28a52ce3e3c9c9dc9a
msgid "Plug in the vehicle's LiPo battery so that both the TX1 and autopilot are powered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:61
#: 45c933f045674aceb7629bfef1df7704
msgid "Connect the autopilot to a ground station using a USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:62
#: 0019d441de974df3b3c193f6721e7d28
msgid "If you are using Mission Planner as your ground station, once messages are successfully passing from the ZED/TX1 to the autopilot: - a proximity viewer should appear showing the distance to objects ahead of the vehicle (if :ref:`PRX1_TYPE <PRX1_TYPE>` was enabled above) - \"Bad Vision Position\" message should disappear from the HUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:65
#: aa0a5c64f1ed48878f6ffaf5f483a237
msgid "Set the home position from the ground station map (from MP's Flight Data screen, right-mouse-button-click on the map and select \"Set EKF Origin Here\").  The vehicle should appear on the map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:70
#: e44b0ce829734a85aa0a91f13b302d0f
msgid "Pick-up the vehicle and walk it around checking that the vehicle's position movements are shown on the map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:73
#: 7adec4c4fe6641ea94b52cbd927fb95e
msgid "Flight testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:75
#: 0a3cf89e71574a4b803bc2ad8d4c7241
msgid "Setup the vehicle with AltHold and Loiter flight modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:76
#: b818b3dcc27e40538a578d63b50fa834
msgid "Setup an :ref:`auxiliary switch <channel-7-and-8-options>` to enable/disable object avoidance and move switch to the off position.  Alternatively set :ref:`PRX1_TYPE <PRX1_TYPE>` to 0.  This helps ensure the vehicle will not backaway from objects in AltHold mode which could surprise the pilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-zed.rst:77
#: 70e43d2382bb49b5aace190ed5b08a6b
msgid "Attempt to arm and take-off in Loiter mode"
msgstr ""

